  "summary": "lodash vulnerable to prototype pollution via array-path bypass in `_.unset`, `_.omit`, and `_.pullAt",
  "details": "### Impact\n\nThe `_.unset`, `_.omit`, and `_.pullAt` functions are vulnerable to prototype pollution. The fix for [CVE-2025-13465](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/security/advisories/GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg) only guards against string key members, so an attacker can bypass the check by passing array-wrapped path segments. This allows deletion of properties from built-in prototypes such as `Object.prototype`, `Number.prototype`, and `String.prototype`.\n\nThe issue permits deletion of prototype properties but does not allow overwriting their original behavior.\n\n### Patches\n\nThe issue is patched from 4.18.0 to 4.18.1 depending on the package: `lodash`, `lodash-es`, and `lodash-amd` in 4.18.1, and the standalone `lodash.unset` and `lodash.omit` packages in 4.18.0.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nNone. Upgrade to the patched version.\n\n### References\n\n- [CVE-2025-13465 / GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg](https://github.com/lodash/lodash/security/advisories/GHSA-xxjr-mmjv-4gpg) (original fix that this bypasses)",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V3",
      "score": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:L"
    }
